I'm currently close to finishing up an extinctionist game... not exactly a
strict extinctionist, but pretty close.

Essentially, to get an extinctionist, you have to kill 120 of every
possible creature, except for those specifically limited (uniques, 9
nazgul, etc.)  There are of course some limits on how far you take this --
killing 120 woodchucks or 120 mail daemons, for example, are optional.
Most extinctionists also leave Izchak alive.  It takes darn near forever.

I have a feeling most "ascendable" characters could go extinctionist.  All
you really need is near-infinite patience, and near-infinite food (slow
digestion, for example.)  It also helps to have an altar fairly deep in
the dungeon so you can sac for spellbooks, golden glows, AC, etc.  Wizards
make good extinctionists, because they can stand there zapping "create
monster" for just about forever, especially with their quest artifact.
Priests are good, as well, though it'd be nice if their quest artifact
gave them more power (~120 isn't much when you have a max of 4000 :P).  It
also helps to have smoky = EH or FH or ObjDet, so you can get lots of
wishes (provided you don't want to play wishless.)

There isn't a lot to it if you know how to ascend -- just make camp near
the castle, and create monster for as long as you can.

As long as you're going extinctionist, you may as well dig out every wall
you can, and zap "light" everywhere.  51 levels of "bigroom" is pretty
impressive ;)



